680}], \"window\": [22831, 51631]}", "latency_ms": 7, "tokens_before": 25763, "tokens_after": 25763, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_85d6791d", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1006, 1860, 1532, 1680, 153], "window": [22831, 51631], "confidence": 0.76, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "1006's out-neighbourhood {1532, 1680} is disjoint from 1860's in-neighbourhood {153, 182, 743, 1390}, so no 2-hop path exists. The only plausible relay, hub 1680, is contacted by 1006 only at t>=46832, whereas 1860's last inbound event (153->1860) occurs by 44431 \u2014 the candidate route runs backwards in time and far exceeds the 600-unit delay budget. 1680 also never contacts 153 within [37232,44431], so its static link to 153 is not time-respecting. The alternative branch through 1532 is a dead end: 1532 is nearly isolated (3 events), its out-contacts (1036, 1643) do not reach 1860, and none of its events fall within 600 units after 1006 contacted it. High overall event volume and 1680's hub status are therefore insufficient to establish a cascade."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure.** 1006 has only 3 events with 3 partners; its out-neighbours are {1532, 1680} (step_02, step_03). 1860 has 5 events; its in-neighbours are {153, 182, 743, 1390} (step_02, step_04). The two neighbour sets are disjoint \u2014 no 2-hop route.\n\n**Timing.** Binning activity (step_08, step_09, step_15):\n- 1006's three events fall at \u2248[37232\u201338431], [40832\u201342031], [46832\u201348031].\n- 1006\u21921680 occurs only in [46832, 49231] (step_11), and *not* earlier (step_10).\n- 1860's activity ends in bin [42032, 44431]; its last inbound event is 153\u21921860 there (step_12).\n\nSo the only high-fan-out route out of 1006 (via hub 1680) opens **\u22484,000+ time units after 1860's last inbound event** \u2014 influence cannot travel backwards in time, let alone within a 600-unit relay limit.\n\n**Confounder controls.**\n- *Popularity of the hub*: 1680 is genuinely a hub (58 events, 51 partners, step_16) and does statically touch 153 (step_07) \u2014 but it never contacts 153 anywhere in [37232, 44431] (step_13), the only interval where such a relay could have preceded 153\u21921860. Static connectivity is therefore not time-respecting.\n- *The other branch*: 1532 is a near-isolated node (3 events, step_16) whose only out-contacts are 1036 and 1643 (step_06) \u2014 neither feeds 1860 \u2014 and none of its events fall in the bins immediately following 1006\u21921532 (step_15), so no \u2264600-unit relay exists there either.\n- *Volume*: the window carries 5,134 events over 1,863 nodes (step_01), so bulk activity alone could superficially suggest connectivity; the per-node timing refutes it.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_85d6791d\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860, 1532, 1680, 153],\n  \"window\": [22831, 51631],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006's out-neighbourhood {1532, 1680} is disjoint from 1860's in-neighbourhood {153, 182, 743, 1390}, so no 2-hop path exists. The only plausible relay, hub 1680, is contacted by 1006 only at t>=46832, whereas 1860's last inbound event (153->1860) occurs by 44431 \u2014 the candidate route runs backwards in time and far exceeds the 600-unit delay budget. 1680 also never contacts 153 within [37232,44431], so its static link to 153 is not time-respecting. The alternative branch through 1532 is a dead end: 1532 is nearly isolated (3 events), its out-contacts (1036, 1643) do not reach 1860, and none of its events fall within 600 units after 1006 contacted it. High overall event volume and 1680's hub status are therefore insufficient to establish a cascade.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 34087, "total_output_tokens": 7101, "total_tokens": 41188, "total_latency_ms": 90408, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}